# Level_Generation_Design — Skeleton

## 1. Applies when
Procedural or hybrid level games (roguelite).

## 2. This document owns
- Generation intent: room/grammar types, constraint rules (connectivity, locks/keys, difficulty budget).
- Generator input parameters and what designers tune vs what is fixed.
- Seeded reproducibility policy and generation QA sampling plan.

## 3. This document does NOT own
- Hand-authored level content — Level_Design.
- Run phase shape — Run_Structure_Design.
- Enemy placement rules — Enemy/Encounter design (they supply constraints).

## 4. Recommended chapter structure
1. Generation philosophy / 2. Room/grammar catalogue / 3. Constraints & solvability / 4. Difficulty budget / 5. Tunable parameters / 6. Seeding & QA sampling / 7. Failure modes / 8. Open questions

## 5. Common boundaries
- Generation vs Level_Design: system here; authored spaces there; hybrid split declared explicitly.
- Constraints from other docs are *inputs*, linked not duplicated.

## 6. Common audit rules
- Every room type lists its allowed exits and lock compatibilities.
- Solvability invariant stated and every constraint traces to it.
